Third-party software that rakun runs
====================================

rakun does not contain this software: it downloads it from the place it comes
from with `rakunctl helpers update` (the versions rakun was tested with, checked
by sha256), and runs it as separate programs. The -full tarballs carry a copy,
with the texts of the licences in the licenses/ folder. `rakunctl helpers` says
which version of each one is installed.

legendary            Epic Games store   https://github.com/legendary-gl/legendary
                     GPL-3.0 (licenses/GPL-3.0.txt)
gogdl                GOG store          https://github.com/Heroic-Games-Launcher/heroic-gogdl
                     GPL-3.0 (licenses/GPL-3.0.txt)
nile                 Amazon Games       https://github.com/imLinguin/nile
                     GPL-3.0 (licenses/GPL-3.0.txt)
umu-launcher         Proton prefixes    https://github.com/Open-Wine-Components/umu-launcher
                     GPL-3.0 (licenses/GPL-3.0.txt)
comet                GOG Galaxy         https://github.com/imLinguin/comet
                     Apache-2.0 (licenses/comet.Apache-2.0.txt)
heroic-epic-integration (EpicGamesLauncher.exe)
                                        https://github.com/BananaWorks07/heroic-epic-integration
                     MIT (licenses/heroic-epic-integration.MIT.txt)
zoom-platform.sh     Zoom Platform      https://zoom-platform.sh/zoom-platform.sh
                     Written by Zoom Platform; downloaded from its own site.
                     It has no licence text that rakun knows of.

The source code of each program is in its repository, at the version rakun uses
(`rakunctl helpers` says which).

The "Rakun" lettering of the web is drawn from the outlines of Lilita One by
Juan Montoreano, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (web/LilitaOne-OFL.txt).
